Z||000000||Phantom Rage||10-03-1999||07:47 PM||||I was just wondering how hard is it to cut into the hood of the fiero. I found some Turbo Sunbird hood louvers.  I am really afraid to mess up my hood. Any tips would be appreciated.  Thx  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-03-1999||11:20 PM||||Whenever you put the louvers in, take pictures! I doubt I'm the only one on here who'd be interested in seeing that project.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rcn491||10-03-1999||11:44 PM||||I cut an opening in mine for my kit car.<BR>It's not hard to do. I used a Dremel tool with a cut off wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||10-04-1999||12:40 AM||||I cut the opening for my rear decklid scoop, it was not a hard job to do. I used a cut-off wheel on a cordless drill and a dremel tool. The scoop covers the hole so it does leave room to play.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||10-04-1999||01:38 AM||||If you use a saber saw, be careful and go slow, those saws have a nasty habit of melting the plastic.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||10-04-1999||08:14 PM||||Saw some Turbo Gran Prix louvers today,aws thinking the same thing.<BR>I'd make sure and stay away from any reinforcement stuff on the underside,if there is any,haven't looked.||||reg||1
